     Did you rebuild nethack after that?  src/tile.c is constructed
during the build process and if you ended up using an old one it
wouldn't reflect the revised tiles data.

> [...] What is the "comment identifying tile"?

     That should probably be "comment which identifies each tile".
It refers to the monster name or the object name & object description
enclosed within parentheses at the start of each tile.  The sequence
number which precedes the name doesn't matter; the text is used to
match up with monst.o and objects.o when constructing `src/tile.c'.


